**Finding: compliant (preferred position).**

The Agreement contains no non-solicitation, no-hire or inducement restriction binding Client. Targeted searches across all sections (including the planner's candidates § 8 Client covenants and § 10 confidentiality, plus § 2, § 7 and § 12) surfaced only:

- § 7 "Unsolicited Commercial E-Mail" — a spam/AUP term, not a personnel restriction;
- § 8(c) — a Client-side access-limitation covenant naming "officers, employees, and agents", which restricts Interface access, not hiring or solicitation;
- § 8(d) — a cross-reference to a separate Non-Competition Agreement limiting Credit Data use, not personnel solicitation.

Because our preferred position is that no non-solicit binds Customer, absence is the best available outcome and no redline was proposed. Noted for negotiation: if TrueLink later introduces such a covenant, we hold at the fallback (mutual, personnel directly involved in the Services, ≤12 months from end of involvement, general-advertisement and unsolicited-approach carve-outs, no no-hire).
